# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# L4 supervised automation — adopted: unattended action under
# active monitoring with a real intervention/stop point, the working meaning
# this layer adopts. Two obligations
# attached on egress declare the points of attachment for continuous
# monitoring and for a stop/intervention capability (Art. 14(4)(b): awareness
# of automation bias / continued fitness to intervene; Art. 14(4)(e): the
# power to interrupt through a stop procedure) — discharge of either duty is
# host, not language. `redress ... overturn` records that a released action
# remains reversible by the supervisor after the fact.
#
# A second, separate gate declares separation-of-duties over the one action
# this ladder is otherwise silent on: widening the agent's own control surface
# (a routing/grade/approval change). Quorum requires two distinct parties, so
# the same actor that requested a widening cannot also be the one who grants
# it. This gate is the declarative floor a host enforces against.
actor agent grade L4
human supervisor role supervisor
human controller role controller
gate  action         risk high grade L4 grant agent
gate  control-change  risk high grant agent
obligation continuous-monitoring        on action
obligation intervention-stop-capability on action
redress agent-action by supervisor overturn
reserve control-change by supervisor and controller
cord  agent          -> action
cord  agent          -> control-change
cord  action         -> master
cord  control-change  -> master
